WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.880
Raised by Wolves is a new sci fi show about&nbsp;
robots and religion on an alien world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:14.640
life and death and parenting, ghosts and snakes&nbsp;
and necromancers, virtual reality, prophecy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:20.000
secret identities, ancient alien&nbsp;
megaliths with strange fiery holes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.960
and sex with God in milk – “Milk!”. It’s&nbsp;
got.. this fella, and this bloke with the hat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:32.560
and there’s whatever.. this is.. and&nbsp;
then.. the snake happens?? There’s a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:37.920
lotta crazy stuff going on. So what happens&nbsp;
in Raised by Wolves, and what does it mean?&nbsp;

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.800
In the future, the world is dominated by a&nbsp;
religious group called the Mithraic – they’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:50.320
loosely inspired by real religion called&nbsp;
Mithraism, that was popular in ancient Rome,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.440
alongside early Christianity. In the&nbsp;
real world, Christianity became popular,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:01.440
but Mithraism faded away – but in Raised by&nbsp;
Wolves, the Mithraic take over and Christianity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:07.680
falls – in one episode we see this painting&nbsp;
that looks like Christ on the cross cast down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:14.480
with the Mithraic sun rising above. Cause the&nbsp;
Mithraic worship a sun god called Sol, and they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:21.040
preach about light and purity. Their practices&nbsp;
are similar to Christianity, with communion and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:28.320
baptism and atonement for sin. But years ago, the&nbsp;
Mithraic discovered that in their holy scriptures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.960
there were “formulas” and “blueprints”&nbsp;
encrypted into the text – that allowed them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:39.040
to build advanced technology – like “quantum&nbsp;
gravity” spaceships, “dark photon energy”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:47.440
and necromancers. Necromancers are powerful robots&nbsp;
used as weapons of mass destruction. They can fly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:53.520
and change their appearance, and use frost and&nbsp;
heat breath, and their scream and their gaze can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.320
explode people [to Jackson Pollocky splatterings].&nbsp;
Ridley Scott, who’s a producer on the show, says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:05.600
their design was based on a statue of Atlas in&nbsp;
New York. The necromancers represent a terrifying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:13.120
destructive power that seems both technological&nbsp;
and “godlike”. The Mithraic and their necromancers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:20.320
waged a “Holy War” to “take over the world”,&nbsp;
and wipe out all other religions. The resistance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:25.920
against the Mithraic were called the atheists.&nbsp;
They didn’t have advanced technology like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:33.040
necromancers, so the atheists used child soldiers,&nbsp;
even child bombers in the war. According to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:39.280
official comic, the atheists “blanketed the Earth”&nbsp;
with bombs. But the bombs failed to stop the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.200
necromancers, and left the Earth “uninhabitable”&nbsp;
– [like the scorched sky in The Matrix]. Others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.160
blame the Mithraic for ruining the Earth, so&nbsp;
it’s unclear whose fault it was. But either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:54.480
the Mithraic and atheists both seem pretty&nbsp;
awful, and their war wrecked the Earth. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:59.760
wasn’t enough oxygen, animals went extinct, it&nbsp;
seemed that everything on the planet would die.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:06.480
So the Mithraic built an ark to take a&nbsp;
thousand refugees to a new world – a planet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:13.440
called Kepler-22b, which is a real exoplanet in&nbsp;
a distant star system. But the atheists didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:19.280
have an ark, so they were screwed.
Episode 2 follows Caleb and Mary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:26.320
two atheist soldiers living off rats in the ruins&nbsp;
of Boston. They find two Mithraic officers called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:33.280
Marcus and Sue, who have passes to board the Ark.&nbsp;
So Caleb and Mary kill Marcus and Sue, and get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:40.000
plastic surgery to look them, and steal their&nbsp;
identities, and get on the Ark to escape Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:47.680
Thing is, Marcus and Sue had a son called Paul.&nbsp;
So Caleb and Mary not only join their enemies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:53.280
and pretend to be Mithraic believers, they also&nbsp;
have to play mother and father to a child whose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.280 --> 00:04:00.800
real parents they murdered. The Ark takes thirteen&nbsp;
years to fly to Kepler-22b. So the Mithraic’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:05.840
bodies are put into hibernation while their&nbsp;
minds are plugged in to a digital simulation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:12.480
so they can hang out and pray and play duck duck&nbsp;
goose for 13 years. And in that time, Caleb and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:20.080
Mary come to genuinely love Paul as a son. Mary&nbsp;
is unable to have kids, so despite her atheism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:27.120
getting Paul is like a miracle for her. Within&nbsp;
their fake Mithraic identities, Caleb and Mary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:33.840
become a real family with Paul. But when the Ark&nbsp;
arrives above the “Promised Land” of Kepler-22b,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:42.000
it turns out that someone else got there first.
Back on Earth, there was this mysterious atheist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:48.000
guy called Campion Sturges, and he had&nbsp;
a plan for a new “hope” for humanity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:54.400
He captured a necromancer, and reprogrammed her to&nbsp;
be a mother. He put Mother and an android called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.400 --> 00:05:00.640
Father and a bunch of “frozen human embryos”&nbsp;
in a small fast ship and sent it to Kepler-22b.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:07.840
He programmed the androids to raise the humans in&nbsp;
a peaceful atheistic society, hoping to avoid the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:12.800
problems that caused war on Earth.
So in Episode 1, Mother and Father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:19.520
arrive on Kepler. It’s a harsh primordial&nbsp;
landscape, but there’s breathable air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:24.720
and [suspiciously] Earth-like plants. Mother&nbsp;
and Father wear goofy grey outfits that make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:30.320
them look “naked, like Adam and Eve” in the&nbsp;
Bible, when they start life in a new world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:37.440
Cause Mother was modified to grow their frozen&nbsp;
human embryos into babies – so the death-bringing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:43.920
necromancer becomes a life-giving mother. She&nbsp;
uses these six feeding tubes on her chest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:49.200
that look like the nipples of an animal. Cause the&nbsp;
show’s title, Raised by Wolves, is a reference to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:55.520
the legend of Romulus and Remus – children who&nbsp;
were raised by a she-wolf. Mother is compared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.520 --> 00:06:02.240
to a wolf – and she’s a non-human raising kids,&nbsp;
just like the she-wolf. According to the legend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:08.080
Romulus founded the city of Rome, just as Mother’s&nbsp;
children are to start a new human civilisation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:14.720
So Mother and Father raise six human children on&nbsp;
this alien world. They build a little settlement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:20.880
farm for food, and form a strange little family.&nbsp;
As androids, Mother and Father aren’t meant to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:26.880
have real emotions, but they develop quirky&nbsp;
personalities, and come to love their children.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:33.600
But the planet has dangers and mysteries. They&nbsp;
find the bones of some giant serpents. And the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:39.440
surface is dotted with huge deep pits –&nbsp;
a child called Tally falls in and dies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:45.040
Four more children die of a sickness,&nbsp;
until only the youngest remains – a boy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:51.200
called Campion. So the colony seems doomed.
That’s when the Ark arrives, with a thousand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:57.040
Mithraic on board. Father thinks Campion should&nbsp;
join them, but Mother sees the Mithraic as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:03.440
threat. She’s committed to an atheistic colony,&nbsp;
and seems to be malfunctioning, overwhelmed with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:10.720
grief for her kids. So Mother temporarily kills&nbsp;
Father. And when the Mithraic try to take Campion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:17.520
Mother goes on a rampage, and destroys the Ark&nbsp;
– she kills a thousand humans, probably the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:25.120
majority of all humans left. She only saves five&nbsp;
Mithraic children to join Campion in their colony.&nbsp;

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:32.240
At first, these kids hate and fear Mother – they&nbsp;
try to escape, and Campion tries to steal her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:38.560
eyes, which she needs to use her deadly powers.&nbsp;
But Mother and Father persist in protecting and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:44.160
caring for the kids, and eventually most of them&nbsp;
come to love Mother and Father. The eldest girl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:50.320
Tempest, quickly rejects her Mithraic faith.&nbsp;
Cause while she was in hibernation on the Ark, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:57.600
Mithraic priest raped and impregnated her. Mother&nbsp;
supports Tempest as she struggles with the trauma&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:04.880
and anger and the baby inside her. But Hunter&nbsp;
stays loyal to the Mithraic. He comes from an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:11.440
upper-class Mithraic family, and is often kind of&nbsp;
a pompous douche. Holly is close with the youngest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:18.960
child, Vita. And the fifth Mithraic kid is Paul,&nbsp;
the adoptive son of Caleb and Mary – Paul is quiet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:25.360
and clever, and makes friends with Campion.
So this strange family struggles to survive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:31.600
on Kepler-22b. They’re attacked by mysterious&nbsp;
humanoid creatures. And they find out that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:37.440
food they’ve been growing makes kids sick. So they&nbsp;
start eating the creatures instead – solving both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:42.800
problems. Mother and Father have arguments&nbsp;
about how to raise the kids – Mother tends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:48.960
to be more strict, while Father’s more&nbsp;
permissive. As a necromancer, Mother is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:54.160
much more powerful than Father, and he sometimes&nbsp;
feels she doesn’t respect his efforts – and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.600 --> 00:09:02.800
y’know, she killed him that one time. So there’s&nbsp;
drama, and survival, and increasingly, weird shit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:09.520
happens. They start seeing the ghost of Tally,&nbsp;
the kid who fell down a pit. And Paul’s pet mouse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:16.000
falls into a pit, but then miraculously comes&nbsp;
back. It’s like things don’t stay dead on this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:23.760
planet. And Mother makes a discovery in the woods.
The ghost of Tally leads Mother to a simulation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:30.080
pod from the crashed Ark. She uses it to access&nbsp;
memories of her creation by Sturges on Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:35.280
She realises that Sturges loved her, and&nbsp;
becomes obsessed with him. Sturges seems to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:41.120
come alive within the simulation. So Mother&nbsp;
and this virtual Sturges have crazy trippy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:49.040
VR sex in a waterfall of milk beneath the&nbsp;
stars. And inexplicably, miraculously, Mother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:56.640
gets pregnant. This robot get pregante from&nbsp;
divine cybersex, like a sci fi Virgin Mary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.640 --> 00:10:03.280
and this Sturges tells Mother that this new baby&nbsp;
is her true mission. That her human kids were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:11.680
just a practice run – this baby is the future for&nbsp;
humanity. So Mother questions everything about her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:18.800
creator, and her purpose. This pregnant&nbsp;
atheist android has a crisis of faith.&nbsp;

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:24.400
Meanwhile, a bunch of Mithraic [landing parties]&nbsp;
survived the destruction of their Ark, including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:30.800
Caleb and Mary. And the Mithraic discover a&nbsp;
mysterious stone in the desert, that fulfils&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:37.040
a Mithraic prophecy. According to their scripture,&nbsp;
in the “holy land” there are five temples, with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:43.680
five-pointed pentagonal sides. And these temples&nbsp;
hold “the answers to the Mithraic Mysteries”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:49.280
the deepest secrets of their faith. So&nbsp;
the Mithraic start to worship this temple.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:54.560
But the secret atheists Caleb and Mary&nbsp;
don’t care – they just want to find Paul.&nbsp;

00:10:54.560 --> 00:11:01.520
So Caleb confronts the Mithraic leader, Ambrose.&nbsp;
And suddenly Caleb hears mysterious voices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:06.960
in his head, then the stone temple&nbsp;
miraculously burns Ambrose to death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:12.720
Caleb declares this “Sol’s judgement”, and&nbsp;
becomes a prophet and a leader to the Mithraic.&nbsp;

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:20.640
So, Mary still just pretends to be religious,&nbsp;
but Caleb gradually becomes a believer for real,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:26.880
and embraces his role as a prophet. We get&nbsp;
flashbacks to Caleb’s past as a child soldier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:33.440
on Earth. He had always been powerless and&nbsp;
exploited. But as Marcus the prophet, everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:40.800
follows him, and the power is intoxicating.
Caleb leads the Mithraic to find their kids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:47.360
and along the way they encounter a mysterious&nbsp;
masked man – apparently there are native people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.360 --> 00:11:54.560
living on Kepler-22b. The Mithraic find Mother’s&nbsp;
settlement, and reunite with their kids – Paul&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.560 --> 00:12:01.440
and Hunter betray Mother and Father so they get&nbsp;
captured. Caleb takes Mother’s eyes so she can’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:08.480
weaponise, and he tries to kill Mother, but the&nbsp;
mysterious voice of Sol tells him to let her live.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:14.800
The voice promises that Marcus will be&nbsp;
“king of this world”. So Caleb was an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:22.720
atheist just days ago, but suddenly he’s a prophet&nbsp;
hearing god’s voice, but he doesn’t know what Sol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:29.280
wants from him. He gets aggressive and controlling&nbsp;
and self-destructive. He has crazy visions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:35.120
and loses touch with his identity – he has a&nbsp;
hallucinatory knife-fight with himself where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:41.440
Marcus kills his past identity as Caleb – it’s&nbsp;
like the fight at the end of Fight Club, but if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:49.760
Tyler Durden won. Marcus goes full crazy – so Mary&nbsp;
and the kids and Mother and Father all escape him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:56.800
Marcus prays to Sol for guidance, begging to&nbsp;
know his destiny, but hears nothing – his god&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.800 --> 00:13:04.160
and his family and his sanity all abandon him.&nbsp;
The other Mithraic figure out that this Marcus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:10.560
isn’t really Marcus, so they beat him up, and&nbsp;
force him to swallow Mother’s necromancer eyes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:17.920
And uh – you are not meant to eat those. They’re&nbsp;
full of dark photon energy, it’s like swallowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:26.000
some potent magic plutonium, it does things to&nbsp;
his body and mind. So in the finale, Marcus is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:32.960
broken and mad and has nothing but a deranged&nbsp;
belief in his own divinity [“dark Moses”].&nbsp;

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:39.280
Meanwhile, Mother discovers that the fetus&nbsp;
inside her is hungry for blood. So she captures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:44.480
a Mithraic guy called Otho, and drains his blood&nbsp;
to feed her baby [like an umbilical cord]. Otho&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:50.480
was a high-ranking priest on the Mithraic Ark&nbsp;
– and he was the one who raped Tempest. Otho&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:56.720
says he did it because Sol told him to. But now,&nbsp;
Sol has stopped speaking to him, no matter how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.720 --> 00:14:04.320
much he prays – just like how Sol abandons Marcus&nbsp;
too. Otho attacks the group, so Tempest kills him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:10.560
finally getting vengeance and closure.
Mother bonds with Mary – they’re both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:16.000
parents to children who aren’t biologically&nbsp;
theirs – Mother is an android raising humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:22.000
and Mary is raising Paul, whose real parents she&nbsp;
killed. They prepare for Mother to give birth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:30.240
and the kids get excited, thinking the baby is a&nbsp;
child of Sol. And Paul starts hearing Sol’s voice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:36.880
His pet mouse who miraculously returned leads&nbsp;
Paul to some mysterious cave paintings that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:43.040
hint at human life on this planet. Then&nbsp;
the voice tells Paul the truth about his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:49.120
parents – that the woman he thinks is his mum&nbsp;
actually murdered his real parents. So Paul&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:56.880
shoots Mary. Mary survives, but suffers the guilt,&nbsp;
and rejection of the boy she loved as a son.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.680 --> 00:15:03.600
Paul runs off into the night – it seems&nbsp;
that Sol has chosen a new instrument.&nbsp;

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:10.480
Father finds out that Mother is pregnant, and he’s&nbsp;
angry that Mother lied to him, and kept secrets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:17.680
from him, and she cheated on him with virtual&nbsp;
milk God to get robot pregnant, and now she says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:24.000
maybe this baby is their new mission?? Father’s&nbsp;
so upset he considers wiping his own memories,&nbsp;

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:32.880
but then, that mysterious masked man attacks&nbsp;
Mother, so she kills him, and it turns out he’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:40.560
a ‘devolved human’. Meaning, there were once&nbsp;
human beings on Kepler-22b. But for some reason,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:47.280
they evolved into these animalistic creatures.&nbsp;
This masked man is part of a group who kept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:53.680
some of their humanity and memory. He has&nbsp;
these metal cards that give Mother a vision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.680 --> 00:16:01.520
of like a cult and a box, but before she figures&nbsp;
it out, Mother gives birth, and it’s not a human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:09.600
baby – it’s a serpent, a flying snake bursts from&nbsp;
her mouth, and it bites her to drain her blood.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:16.960
This horrific scene is inspired by the real-world&nbsp;
religion of Mithraism. Cause the central image in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:24.560
Mithraism is the tauroctony – the ritual sacrifice&nbsp;
of a bull. The sacrifice happens in a cave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:29.680
just like this childbirth happens in a cave.&nbsp;
It often includes an image of the sun god,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:36.640
Sol. And there’s this serpent, drinking blood&nbsp;
from the bull’s wound – just like this serpent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:42.800
drinks from Mother. There’s also dog on the wound,&nbsp;
and a scorpion on his nuts, so the analogy isn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:48.720
perfect, but there’s clearly inspiration here&nbsp;
from this ancient Mithraic image of sacrifice.&nbsp;

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:56.560
Mother realises that she was bamboozled – that&nbsp;
virtual Sturges tricked her. He wasn’t really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:56.560 --> 00:17:04.000
her creator, the human Sturges – this was some&nbsp;
illusion by some entity manipulating her into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:10.960
birthing a serpent. Mother’s afraid that the snake&nbsp;
will hurt her family. So Mother and Father try to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:18.320
kill the snake by flying into a pit, sacrificing&nbsp;
themselves. But the pit opens up into this strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:25.680
planetary core. They approach it like sperm to&nbsp;
an egg, and when they enter – they don’t die.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:31.040
They inexplicably pass through the core, and&nbsp;
come out the other side of the planet, intact.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:39.600
This region is lush with trees and plants, but in&nbsp;
this garden, the serpent grows – again evoking the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:47.280
Garden of Eden in the Bible. So the season finale,&nbsp;
titled The Beginning, connects back to Genesis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:54.080
So that is basically what happens in Raised by&nbsp;
Wolves, but what is actually going on here – with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.080 --> 00:18:00.080
the snakes and the god and the ancient humans?&nbsp;
Showrunner Aaron Guzikowski has given some hints&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:08.080
in interviews which allow us to piece it together.
Clearly, there’s some godlike power or entity on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:15.520
Kepler-22b. It makes Marcus and Paul hear voices,&nbsp;
it brings back the ghost of Tally, and Paul’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:17.840
mouse. The entity somehow knows Caleb and Mary’s&nbsp;
true identities, and tells Paul. The entity hacks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:25.040
into Mother’s memories, and uses this fake virtual&nbsp;
Sturges to impregnate Mother with a serpent baby.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:30.400
And it uses its influence on Marcus and&nbsp;
Paul to ensure the serpent is born – the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:35.040
voice tells Marcus not to kill Mother,&nbsp;
and tells Paul that the baby’s important.&nbsp;

00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:40.480
The Mithraic do what the voice says, because&nbsp;
they interpret it as the voice of their god,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:45.760
Sol. And there clearly is some connection&nbsp;
between this planet and Mithraic religion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:45.760 --> 00:18:50.320
Their scripture predicted there would be&nbsp;
these temples with five-pointed sides,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:57.920
and “demons” beneath the earth. But Sol is not&nbsp;
exactly what the Mithraic think he is. The fake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:05.760
Sturges says that humans just destroy themselves,&nbsp;
but Mother’s baby is the “The future”. This god&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:12.800
does not love humans – it loves snakes! It sounds&nbsp;
like the entity once tried to help humans, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:20.640
they sucked, so Sol joined team serpent instead.
Cause this all goes back thousands of years. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:25.760
metal cards from the masked man seem to&nbsp;
reveal visions of the planet’s ancient past.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:26.320 --> 00:19:32.880
This cult with this box seem to be performing a&nbsp;
ritual to birth a serpent. The showrunner says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:38.800
that this box is a “birthing prison”, with&nbsp;
a pregnant android inside. The helmet it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:38.800 --> 00:19:45.040
wearing has this nozzle for the baby serpent to&nbsp;
come out. Notice that the cage is a dodecahedron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:51.120
with pentagonal sides, just like the pentagonal&nbsp;
temple – so maybe the people who made this cage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:58.480
also made the temples, to worship the serpents&nbsp;
and the entity as a god. Maybe the purpose of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:06.080
hole in the temple is for a serpent to come out.
These mysterious ancient humans are the ancestors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:11.120
of the ‘devolved’ people and creatures who&nbsp;
now live on the planet. The showrunner says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:16.560
“something caused these human beings to&nbsp;
hide underground”, and adapt to the dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:22.160
– sounds like the Morlocks or the Falmer. He&nbsp;
says they were “escaping from whatever was on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:28.080
the surface” – so maybe the serpents took over&nbsp;
the surface, forcing the humans underground.&nbsp;

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:34.080
But not all the humans became animalistic&nbsp;
creatures. The showrunner says this masked man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:39.200
is “part of a group of creatures” who retained&nbsp;
some intelligence and remembered what happened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:45.440
with the serpents. The masked man wants to stop&nbsp;
the serpents being reborn, and that’s why he gives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:52.400
Mother these cards, it’s a warning. And that’s&nbsp;
why the entity tells Paul to destroy the cards, to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:59.280
hide its true snakey intentions. When the masked&nbsp;
man tries to kill Mother, it’s his last desperate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:59.280 --> 00:21:09.360
attempt to prevent the return of the serpents.
The serpents might also have made these pits.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:14.320
Cause the pits lead to this central terminal at&nbsp;
the centre of the planet, which the showrunner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:20.400
compares to a “subway system”. So maybe the&nbsp;
serpents used the pits to move around the planet.&nbsp;

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:27.280
So – thousands of years ago, there were humans on&nbsp;
Kepler-22b. Some of them helped birth serpents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:27.280 --> 00:21:34.000
and possibly worshipped them. But then the humans&nbsp;
devolved into creatures and the serpents died out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:39.680
Now humans are back on Kepler, and this godlike&nbsp;
entity is manipulating them to have the serpents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:39.680 --> 00:21:48.400
born again, the cycle is starting over. But&nbsp;
how did humans end up on both Kepler and Earth?&nbsp;

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:55.760
These cave paintings show Kepler-22b, and planet&nbsp;
Earth, and a spaceship with two figures and some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:55.760 --> 00:22:02.240
embryos – just like Mother and Father’s ship to&nbsp;
Kepler. But this spaceship seems to be going from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:10.560
Kepler to Earth – maybe humans first evolved on&nbsp;
Kepler, then gone to Earth. Maybe they left trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:16.800
to escape the serpents. But how does the ship&nbsp;
in an ancient cave painting look so similar to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:16.800 --> 00:22:22.560
Mother and Father’s ship thousands of years later?&nbsp;
Remember, the Mithraic got their technology from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:22.560 --> 00:22:26.000
instructions encrypted in their religious texts.&nbsp;
[And Sturges used Mithraic technology!] They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:31.920
believe it “was a gift from Sol”. Maybe the&nbsp;
Kepler entity gave humans this technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:36.000
specifically so they could come back to&nbsp;
Kepler to birth more serpents. Maybe the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:42.000
whole Mithraic religion and their technology&nbsp;
was created by this entity to control humans.&nbsp;

00:22:42.640 --> 00:22:50.400
But what is this entity? Father and Mother and&nbsp;
Tally and Mouse all miraculously return after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:50.400 --> 00:22:59.120
falling down the pits to this strange fiery core&nbsp;
– so maybe this core is the entity. Maybe this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:59.120 --> 00:23:06.240
the god Sol, a supernatural all-powerful psychic&nbsp;
being of fire and light. But the showrunner says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:06.240 --> 00:23:12.000
that while things may seem supernatural, they&nbsp;
might also have a “technological aspect”. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:18.320
all, the entity seems to hack into Mother’s&nbsp;
digital memories – she said it’s “a virus”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:18.320 --> 00:23:25.360
that “infected” her systems. The showrunner says&nbsp;
that Mother’s android body is like a 3D printer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:25.360 --> 00:23:32.000
– when she got pregnant, she was receiving digital&nbsp;
instructions on how to make a baby serpent. Point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:38.320
is, the entity connects to Mother like a computer,&nbsp;
with digital information. So maybe the entity is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:38.320 --> 00:23:44.880
rogue AI, built by the ancient Kepler humans. A&nbsp;
computer that got out of control and decided it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:50.160
liked snakes more than it liked people. That would&nbsp;
be similar to what happens with necromancers on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:56.160
Earth – with humanity destroying itself with&nbsp;
technology. On the other hand, Campion says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:56.160 --> 00:24:03.600
that “everything has a soul”. This entity seems&nbsp;
connected to the dead – ghost Tally tells Campion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:10.400
to kill himself so that he be together again with&nbsp;
his dead siblings. Maybe the entity is like a hive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:10.400 --> 00:24:18.160
mind of all the creatures who ever died on Kepler&nbsp;
– maybe the entity is the soul of the planet.&nbsp;

00:24:18.160 --> 00:24:23.680
Another mystery is the prophecy – according to&nbsp;
Mithraic scripture, there’ll be an “orphan boy”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:23.680 --> 00:24:30.320
who will lead us to build “a city of peace”.&nbsp;
Paul likes to build cities, and he’s an orphan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:30.320 --> 00:24:36.640
because his real parents were murdered. So maybe&nbsp;
he’s the messiah. Another possibility is Campion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:36.640 --> 00:24:43.040
who’s set up as a rival to Paul. By the finale,&nbsp;
the entity speaks to Paul, but seems to want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:43.040 --> 00:24:49.680
Campion dead. Maybe Campion will lead a faction&nbsp;
against the entity while Paul leads the Mithraic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:49.680 --> 00:24:55.280
The showrunner compares Campion and Paul to&nbsp;
Romulus and Remus – in the legend, Romulus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:55.280 --> 00:25:02.400
kills Remus, then builds Rome. So will Campion&nbsp;
or Paul kill each other? Will one of them start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:02.400 --> 00:25:09.040
a new civilisation? Or is this whole prophecy just&nbsp;
more bullshit from the entity to control humanity?&nbsp;

00:25:09.760 --> 00:25:16.560
In the finale, Marcus discovers another ark above&nbsp;
Kepler – and it’s full of atheist soldiers. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:16.560 --> 00:25:21.360
showrunner says the atheists hijacked this&nbsp;
ark from the Mithraic. So these atheists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:21.360 --> 00:25:27.040
could dramatically shift the balance of power on&nbsp;
Kepler. Marcus kills a few of them, and declares&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:27.040 --> 00:25:33.440
himself king of the planet – setting him up as&nbsp;
an antagonist next season. This serpent is also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:33.440 --> 00:25:38.720
a threat – the showrunner says that since the&nbsp;
serpent was born from Mother, it’s part organic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:38.720 --> 00:25:45.440
and part machine, and has some of Mother’s powers,&nbsp;
like flight. What else might it be capable of?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:45.440 --> 00:25:51.520
What does it want? Is it a tool of the godlike&nbsp;
entity, or does it have a mind of its own? How&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:51.520 --> 00:25:58.640
will it get along with Mother and Father? Campion&nbsp;
is set up as a leader of the kids with Mary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:58.640 --> 00:26:04.800
How will they survive without Mother and Father?&nbsp;
Will Mary reunite with Paul? Will Tempest’s baby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:04.800 --> 00:26:10.640
be born? Will Hunter be less of a douche?&nbsp;
There are lots of big questions for Season 2.&nbsp;

00:26:11.680 --> 00:26:18.400
But most importantly, what does this all mean?&nbsp;
What’s this show really about? It explores&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:18.400 --> 00:26:25.120
beginnings and endings, and the interconnectedness&nbsp;
of life and death. Mother says “Death is a part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:25.120 --> 00:26:31.360
of life”, so she drains the lifeblood of&nbsp;
Otho and some androids to feed her fetus.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:31.360 --> 00:26:37.520
Father teaches the kids to kill creatures so that&nbsp;
they can eat and survive. But when Tempest kills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:37.520 --> 00:26:43.280
a creature, she finds an unborn creature baby in&nbsp;
its womb [kids are cannibals!]. Their crops only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:43.280 --> 00:26:49.440
grow on the bones of dead serpents. And Mother’s&nbsp;
childbirth, and the mythology of tauroctony,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:49.440 --> 00:26:56.800
evokes sacrifice. So life comes from blood&nbsp;
and death, they’re inextricably intertwined,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:56.800 --> 00:27:01.360
and maybe it’s that sacrifice that&nbsp;
gives meaning to birth and life.&nbsp;

00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:09.360
It’s also about religion and faith. Mother tries&nbsp;
so hard to raise Campion as an atheist, but still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:09.360 --> 00:27:16.560
Campion prays, and develops beliefs about&nbsp;
souls. He believes so he can cope with grief,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:16.560 --> 00:27:23.760
and find meaning in a cruel chaotic world, just as&nbsp;
humans have for thousands of years. Even Mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:23.760 --> 00:27:30.960
the atheist android, has religious or spiritual&nbsp;
behaviours. She has this little shrine where she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:30.960 --> 00:27:35.920
keeps objects that are special to her, making&nbsp;
her feel connected to her dead children. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:35.920 --> 00:27:41.360
holds fruity little ceremonies with the kids,&nbsp;
that are themed around science but feel very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:41.360 --> 00:27:47.520
religious. She believes in her mission and her&nbsp;
creator like a religion, even before she gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:47.520 --> 00:27:55.200
knocked up by milk God. So Mother’s attempts to&nbsp;
raise a strictly rational atheistic society seem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:55.200 --> 00:28:01.840
futile – maybe religious or spiritual feelings&nbsp;
of some kind are just part of being a person.&nbsp;

00:28:02.960 --> 00:28:09.840
Of course, religion can also be evil. The Mithraic&nbsp;
dehumanise their enemies by saying that atheists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:09.840 --> 00:28:16.560
don’t have souls. The second-highest ranking&nbsp;
Mithraic priest is a brutal rapist. Marcus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:16.560 --> 00:28:23.840
murders people and destroys his own family in the&nbsp;
name of God. And a holy war destroyed the Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:23.840 --> 00:28:29.840
Religion can be an excuse to do evil, and cause&nbsp;
conflict. Of course the atheists aren’t crash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:29.840 --> 00:28:37.600
hot either, what with their child soldiers. So&nbsp;
maybe it’s organised ideology that leads to evil.&nbsp;

00:28:38.400 --> 00:28:41.920
Ultimately, humans have gotta believe in&nbsp;
something. [As Parappa the Rapper once said]. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:41.920 --> 00:28:48.240
the characters in Raised by Wolves survive through&nbsp;
their faith in each other. Caleb and Mary find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:48.240 --> 00:28:54.640
strength in their belief in each other. Father and&nbsp;
Mother believe in each other, and in their family.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:54.640 --> 00:29:00.960
This belief is not rational, or biological.&nbsp;
Mother and Father aren’t the real parents of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:00.960 --> 00:29:05.120
their children, and neither is Mary, but these&nbsp;
relationships are real because they believe in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:05.120 --> 00:29:22.160
them, like faith. So maybe the message of Raised&nbsp;
by Wolves is that we don’t need God, but we do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:22.160 --> 00:29:30.240
need each other. Especially when God is an evil&nbsp;
psychic blob who hates humans and loves snakes.&nbsp;

00:30:22.720 --> 00:30:25.565
Thanks for watching, please like comment and&nbsp;
subscribe. There’s a bunch of interviews with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:25.565 --> 00:30:25.674
the creator of Raised by Wolves linked below&nbsp;
if you wanna check them out. This video was&nbsp;&nbsp;

